# Frontend Architecture Rules

- Use Next.js App Router.
- Server Components are the default.
- Keep Client Components limited to genuine interaction.
- Do not place `"use client"` on root layouts, full pages, static content sections, or footers.
- Keep content local, typed, readonly, and build-time validated.
- Use strict TypeScript. No `any`, `@ts-ignore`, blind assertions, or broad lint disables.
- Use `satisfies` for content collections.
- Use path-based `en` and `ko` locale routing.
- Use static dictionary imports and `generateStaticParams()`.
- Language switching must preserve equivalent paths and project slugs.
- Do not add a database, CMS, runtime GitHub API, authentication, analytics, or unnecessary backend.
- Approved UI stack: Tailwind CSS v4, Motion for React, Lucide React.
- Do not add shadcn/ui, Radix, Material UI, Chakra, Bootstrap, another animation library, another icon library, carousel package, Three.js, or particles without documenting an unavoidable reason.
- Use Motion with `LazyMotion`, `domAnimation`, `strict`, and `MotionConfig reducedMotion="user"`.
- Use named Lucide imports.
- Use `next/image` and `next/font`.
- Avoid unnecessary `useEffect`.
